  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a budget of $2M approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule and a breakthrough in predictive analytics during Phase Two. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Training programs with a budget of $15,000 have been approved for the coding team and project managers. The project is currently moving into the development phase, with user interface enhancements planned for October and a detailed report on Phase Two progress to be shared in a staff meeting on November 20th."
